The mount table on WitOS (plan step C1.2): System.Native enumerates mount points for DriveInfo.GetDrives() and
Environment.GetLogicalDrives() from /proc/mounts on Linux, which WitOS does not have (no procfs is ever emulated).
The system layer's libc serves the mount table as /etc/mtab in mntent form, from the mount points the namespace
service names, so the TARGET_WITOS branch opens that file where Linux opens /proc/mounts; the parsing is upstream's.
No configure check or runtime knob covers the path, so this is RFC 0015 section 4's third preference, a branch beside
the other platforms'.

--- a/src/native/libs/System.Native/pal_mount.c
+++ b/src/native/libs/System.Native/pal_mount.c
@@ -137,7 +137,12 @@

 #else
